{
  "id": "WaSendMsg0000001",
  "name": "META-WA-SEND-MESSAGE",
  "active": false,
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "5f119d7a-fca7-5776-9f53-f4af703c642d",
      "name": "Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## META-WA-SEND-MESSAGE\nInput: `wa_id`, `text`, `idempotency_key`, `requested_by`, optional `context_wamid`, optional `document` (TASK 10: `{ link, filename }`, a short signed storage link; `text` is its caption, ≤ 1024. v1.28: n8n reads the file from the link inside office_net, uploads it to Meta (/media) and sends it by its media id, so storage is never public; when the upload fails the link itself is sent, as before), optional `interactive` (TASK 08: `{ kind: buttons|list, button?, choices: [{id, title}] }`; buttons ≤ 3 with titles ≤ 20, a list ≤ 10 rows with titles ≤ 24; `text` is its body, ≤ 1024). The words all come from the API; this only builds Meta's JSON.\nOutput: `{ ok, outbound_id, wamid, status, error_code, error_message }`.\nNever sends twice for the same idempotency key. Refuses (OUTSIDE_24H_WINDOW) without calling Meta when the client has not written in the last 24 hours: use META-WA-SEND-TEMPLATE.\nRetries: one retry after 3 s only for HTTP 429/502/503/504. No retry after a timeout or HTTP 500 (Meta may already have sent it): the result is NETWORK_OR_UNKNOWN / META_ERROR and the caller decides.\nDry run (`whatsapp.dry_run = true`, tests only): recorded as sent with wamid.DRYRUN-<outbound_id>, Meta is never called.",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 520
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "d5e01f1b-1f6c-5aad-a6ef-d2b347bab488",
